# =============================================================================
# WHAT THE BUILD ACTUALLY READS
# =============================================================================
# The context is ~250 MB, of which ~235 MB is static/ -- the media the site
# serves, and the one thing here that is genuinely too big to exclude. Everything
# below is excluded because nothing in `vite build` opens it. Verified against the
# real import graph: zero references from src/ to any of these paths.
#
# Consequence worth stating: this file is part of the build. `bun run build`
# passes locally while `docker build` fails, or the other way round, is a bug in
# HERE -- not in the Dockerfile and not in the app.

# =============================================================================
# Installed and generated -- never in a build context
# =============================================================================
node_modules
.svelte-kit
build
.output
.git

# =============================================================================
# Secrets
# =============================================================================
# The real .env must never reach a build context, even a fake one: `ARG` and
# `ENV` values live in the image history. The negations keep the tracked example
# available, because it is the contract every developer copies from.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# =============================================================================
# Generated during the build
# =============================================================================
# paraglide-js compiles the message files in buildStart(), with `enforce: 'pre'`,
# so a clean checkout builds without this directory. Excluding it here is what
# makes a LOCAL `docker build` produce the same image as CI -- otherwise a stale
# copy from an older paraglide version rides along and gets compiled in.
src/lib/paraglide/

# inlang's own download cache for locale data. Same reasoning, same effect: a
# populated cache locally is what makes a local build quietly differ from CI.
project.inlang/cache

# =============================================================================
# Documentation and authoring workspace
# =============================================================================
# NOTE ON GLOBS: Docker compiles a bare `*` to `[^/]*`, so `*.md` matches markdown
# at the ROOT ONLY and silently leaves every nested file in the context. `**/*.md`
# is the form that means what it looks like.
#
# Safe here because there are no .svx files, `.md` is not in kit.extensions, and
# src/lib/content-kogaion-scraped.md is imported by nothing.
**/*.md
!README.md

# The blog authoring pipeline: .docx sources, generated markdown and the reference
# JSON. ~13.5 MB, and no route imports any of it. Removing it also removes the
# temptation to believe a .docx under blogs/ has anything to do with the site.
blogs/
docs/
tools/
_crawl-report/

# =============================================================================
# Editors and OS
# =============================================================================
.cursor
.gemini
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Vite writes a timestamped copy of the config while the dev server is running.
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*
vite.config.js.timestamp-*